## clinically-informed-support-with-you-at-the-centre | Why Clients Choose MBP | Clinically Informed Support, With You at the Centre | Why Clients Choose MBP – Clinically Informed Support, With You at the Centre
Michelle Barratt Psychology & Administration Services (MBP) provides a welcoming, neutral, and professionally managed entry point for individuals and families seeking psychological and allied health care.
- Clinically Informed Intake: Sensitive, unhurried intake processes help us understand your circumstances and identify a suitable support pathway.
- Appropriate Practitioner Matching: We connect you with clinical psychologists, general psychologists, social workers, or counsellors whose experience aligns with grief, loss, and trauma-informed care.
- Coordinated Care: Where appropriate and with your consent, practitioners can liaise with your GP and other health professionals involved in your care.
- Practical Referral Support: Our team assists with GP referral requirements, Mental Health Treatment Plans, and Medicare-related paperwork where applicable.
- Flexible Access: In-person appointments are available at our Brisbane clinics in Toowong and Manly West, alongside secure Online Therapy / Telehealth Australia-wide where clinically appropriate.
## you-dont-have-to-carry-grief-alone | Start with a Conversation | You Don't Have to Carry Grief Alone | Start with a Conversation – You Don't Have to Carry Grief Alone
You may not be sure what you need right now, or how to put words to what you have been going through.
If loss has left everyday life feeling heavier than it should and you would like a gentle, non-judgmental space to be heard, reaching out can be a helpful first step.
Tell us a little about what has been happening for you, and we will help you explore an appropriate pathway forward.
Contact Michelle Barratt Psychology on (07) 3185 0040 or reach out via our online contact form to learn more about grief, loss, and trauma therapy support.
(If you are ever in immediate danger or experiencing severe distress, please contact emergency services on 000 or reach out to Lifeline on 13 11 14 or Griefline on 1300 845 745 for confidential support.)
